{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1769","id":4159712626,"node_id":"PR_kwDOO5D6p8738C1y","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1769","diff_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1769.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1769.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1769","number":1769,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[codex] Build future-only ProducerConfig and custody primitives","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nIntroduces the future-only semantic KG producer seam required by KG-N1:\n\n- adds an immutable, recursively frozen `ProducerConfig` covering paper/Family scope, release/schema identity, predecessor custody, all input/output paths, canonical serialization, custody metadata, a Family delta callback, status boundaries, and release intent;\n- adds producer-only canonical byte, SHA-256/length, bounded path, raw predecessor authentication, manifest-record, and rollback-journaled local output primitives;\n- rejects resolved-target input/output overlaps and duplicate outputs at config construction, before preparation, and before commit so symlink aliases cannot overwrite custody inputs;\n- binds builds to the resolved producer root, exact receipts for every declared input, and an immutable callback implementation/state digest;\n- invokes the callback with a reduced path-free immutable producer context, opaque-keyed authenticated input bytes/documents, and a path-free predecessor view, while explicitly treating code review—not same-process Python arguments—as the authority boundary;\n- admits only registry-bound checked-in provider identities/source paths and binds/revalidates their exact source SHA-256 and byte length in immutable config;\n- binds deterministic callback primitives, rejects unordered set construction, normalizes non-semantic evidence collections, preserves explicit procedure/step ordering, and proves complete packet hashes across three `PYTHONHASHSEED` values;\n- authenticates build path sets, canonical documents, raw bytes, receipts, and manifest output records before creating temporary files, rejects ancestor/descendant output collisions, and commits artifacts as readable `0644` files;\n- deterministically rebuilds and byte-compares the complete delta/projection/manifest packet before preparation, rejecting coordinated document/receipt/manifest rewrites without changing existing outputs;\n- rolls back every recoverable preexisting byte/mode and removes newly created outputs if a later output path drifts or replacement fails; rollback continues across obstructions and retains/reports authenticated backups that cannot be restored;\n- adds one synthetic non-authoritative future Family fixture that consumes its declared family source through the authenticated payload and produces deterministic delta/projection/manifest bytes without loading or mutating historical Family modules;\n- documents the future producer/runtime independence boundary and exact predecessor binding.\n\n## Why\n\nThe accepted KG-N0 baseline showed that current P1/P3 releases are correct but late historical builders depend on predecessor-module mutation and repeated cumulative orchestration. Copying that implementation pattern into another Paper would increase custody and scaling risk.\n\nThis change provides a bounded replacement seam for future Papers while preserving all admitted P1/P3 bytes and leaving runtime raw-byte verification independent.\n\n## Exact predecessor binding\n\n```text\nbase commit = c68a5e8110278dcff43a3afb4380d7d646491e32\nbase tree = 37994647c2da664dd9b5d1179c8c6b61850e5666\npredecessor issue = #1765\npredecessor PR = #1768\nhead commit = 36f85ec2b8af5e9665b1d6c5deefa1e5a0f2547b\nhead tree = 5651bcf744e034239c252ded1279854195376cb2\n```\n\n## Custody and scope receipts\n\n```text\nhistorical_builder_modified_count = 0\nhistorical_artifact_byte_change_count = 0\nfuture_predecessor_global_mutation_count = 0\nfuture_config_post_construction_mutation_count = 0\nproducer_runtime_validator_implementation_sharing_count = 0\nsemantic_authority_output_count = 0\nruntime_validator_modified_count = 0\nremote_write_count = 0\n```\n\nThe fixture is terminal, local-only, explicitly non-authoritative, and uses only `fixture:` identities. Active intent is rejected unless immutable custody metadata explicitly declares a semantic-authority output.\n\n## Verification\n\n```text\npython3 scripts/vlm/__tests__/issue_1766_future_semantic_kg_producer.test.py\n  PASS — 28/28, including explicit source admission, caller-frame rejection,\n  three-seed determinism, declared-input consumption, coordinated-build rejection,\n  transactional rollback, and obstructed-backup preservation\n\nnode --test scripts/vlm/__tests__/issue_1765_kg_n0_golden_compatibility.test.mjs\n  PASS — 8/8, including deterministic historical replay and byte/mtime zero-write\n\npython3 scripts/vlm/issue_1765_kg_n0_scaling_baseline.py --check\n  PASS\n\nnpm run lint:changed\n  PASS — no changed JS/JSX files\n\ngit diff --check\n  PASS\n```\n\nCloses #1766.\n","created_at":"2026-07-29T10:54:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T12:11:42Z","closed_at":"2026-07-29T11:40:55Z","merged_at":"2026-07-29T11:40:55Z","merge_commit_sha":"1b18c10ccf3762df82aff886d8b790c88c9a9564","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1769/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1769/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1769/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/statuses/36f85ec2b8af5e9665b1d6c5deefa1e5a0f2547b","head":{"label":"Samsen879:task/1766-kg-n1-producer-config","ref":"task/1766-kg-n1-producer-config","sha":"36f85ec2b8af5e9665b1d6c5deefa1e5a0f2547b","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":